{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795222,"nonce":"EhKcGQ2jaK7O1g4QhLxKZuhgxQ0=","title":"Authorize and manage Cloudflare SFU sessions, tracks and TURN lifecycle","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P2\n\nScope\nImplement server-side SFU session creation/negotiation, ordered per-session mutations, authorized track catalog, publish/subscribe permissions, TURN configuration and actual resource cleanup. Keep app secrets backend-only and correlate session/track ownership with a room and billing owner. Handle partial success, uncertain responses, expiry, replacement, reconnect and orphaned tracks. Make revocation/leave/budget exhaustion close existing resources rather than only deleting discovery entries.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nTests cover duplicate/late API responses, per-item failures, stale publisher IDs, transient network loss, kicked users, revoked consent and closed-room resources. A client cannot subscribe to another room's tracks with known identifiers. Call lifecycle recovery is bounded, media never traverses the room WebSocket, and all resource IDs remain attributable for metering/cleanup.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}